    {
      "type": "explain",
      "id": "e1",
      "title": "Want, can, and would like",
      "body": "Vouloir means “to want”; pouvoir means “can” or “to be able to.” Put the second verb in its infinitive form after them: je peux commander. For an order, je voudrais is the softer, more polite form of “I would like.” Learn it as a useful phrase; you do not need to build the whole conditional tense now."
    },
    {
